(function(E){ const x = E["hr-m6"] = E["hr-m6"] || {units:{}}; x.units["hr-6-2"] = {"explain":{"id":"c-hr-6-2-e","course":"hr","unit":"hr-6-2","type":"explain","level":"B1","title":{"en":"Negotiating an offer","tr":"Teklif pazarlığı","fa":"مذاکره بر سر پیشنهاد کار"},"objective":{"en":"After this lesson, you can negotiate salary and terms: make firm offers and test ideas without promising.","tr":"Bu dersin sonunda maaş ve koşullar üzerine pazarlık yapabileceksin: kesin teklif verip söz vermeden fikirleri deneyebileceksin.","fa":"بعد از این درس می‌توانی درباره‌ی حقوق و شرایط مذاکره کنی: پیشنهاد قطعی بدهی و بدون قول دادن ایده‌ها را محک بزنی."},"hook":{"en":"Test an idea before you promise it. In a pay talk, a careless yes is a promise you may not keep. Hana asked for 8,500. Leyla could not say yes, so she tested an idea instead: 'If we..., would that help?'","tr":"Söz vermeden önce fikri sına. Maaş konuşmasında dikkatsiz bir evet, tutamayabileceğin bir sözdür. Hana 8.500 istedi. Leyla evet diyemezdi; bunun yerine bir fikri denedi: 'If we..., would that help?'","fa":"قبل از قول دادن، ایده را امتحان کن. در گفتگوی حقوق، یک «بله»ی بی‌فکر قولی است که شاید نتوانی به آن عمل کنی. هانا ۸٬۵۰۰ خواست. لیلا نمی‌توانست بله بگوید؛ پس به‌جایش ایده‌ای را امتحان کرد: «⁨If we..., would that help?⁩»"},"before":{"en":"Write the email that confirms what you agreed in a pay talk: each term in one sentence, then the next step.","tr":"Bir maaş görüşmesinde anlaştığınız şeyleri teyit eden e-postayı yaz: her şart için bir cümle, sonra bir sonraki adım.","fa":"ایمیلی بنویس که توافق‌های یک گفتگوی حقوق را تأیید کند: هر شرط در یک جمله و بعد قدم بعدی."},"rounds":[[1,4],[2,3]],"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Key points","tr":"Ana nokta","fa":"نکته‌ی اصلی"},"value":"4"},{"label":{"en":"Key phrases","tr":"Anahtar ifade","fa":"عبارت کلیدی"},"value":"3"},{"label":{"en":"Practice tasks","tr":"Alıştırma","fa":"تمرین"},"value":"4"}],"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"The skill","tr":"Beceri","fa":"مهارت"},"head":{"en":"Test an idea before you promise it","tr":"Söz vermeden önce fikri sına","fa":"قبل از قول دادن، ایده را امتحان کن"},"body":{"en":"You can't always say yes at once. So keep two kinds of sentence apart: an idea you are testing, and a promise you will keep. Then confirm the deal in writing.","tr":"Her zaman hemen evet diyemezsin. Bu yüzden iki tür cümleyi ayrı tut: denediğin bir fikir ve tutacağın bir söz. Sonra anlaşmayı yazılı olarak teyit et.","fa":"همیشه نمی‌توانی فوری بله بگویی. پس دو نوع جمله را از هم جدا نگه دار: ایده‌ای که امتحان می‌کنی و قولی که به آن عمل می‌کنی. بعد توافق را کتبی تأیید کن."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The language","tr":"Dil","fa":"زبان"},"head":{"en":"Firm offers and tentative proposals: if + will, if + would","tr":"Kesin teklifler ve temkinli öneriler: if + will, if + would","fa":"پیشنهاد قطعی و پیشنهاد آزمایشی: if با will، if با would"},"steps":[{"en":"Firm offer: If + present, will + verb.","tr":"Kesin teklif: If + present, will + fiil.","fa":"برای پیشنهاد قطعی، در بخش if حال ساده بیاور و در بخش دیگر will و فعل ساده.","ex":"If you start on 1 January, we will pay for the course."},{"en":"Testing an idea: If + past, would + verb?","tr":"Bir fikri denemek: If + past, would + fiil?","fa":"برای امتحان کردن یک ایده، در بخش if گذشته بیاور و در بخش دیگر would و فعل ساده.","ex":"If we offered 8,500, would you accept it?"},{"en":"No will or would in the if-part.","tr":"if kısmında will ya da would olmaz.","fa":"در بخش if نه will می‌آید نه ⁨would⁩.","ex":"If you start..., not If you will start..."}],"table":{"headers":{"en":["Job","Pattern","Example"],"tr":["İşlev","Kalıp","Örnek"],"fa":["کاربرد","الگو","مثال"]},"rows":[["Firm offer","If + present, will + verb","If you start on 1 January, we will pay for the course."],["Tentative proposal","If + past, would + verb","If we offered 8,500, would you accept it?"],["Showing you listened","I see where you're coming from.","I see where you're coming from, but..."]]},"tip":{"en":"Persian and Turkish make the same firm vs tentative difference (agar bedahim / agar midadim), so the idea is familiar. In English, will marks the firm offer and would the tentative one.","tr":"Türkçede de fark var: 'Başlarsan öderiz' (kesin) ve '8.500 versek kabul eder miydin?' (deneme). İngilizcede bu farkı will ve would taşır.","fa":"فارسی هم همین تفاوت را دارد: «اگر ۸٬۵۰۰ بدهیم، قبول می‌کنید؟» (قطعی‌تر) و «اگر ۸٬۵۰۰ می‌دادیم، قبول می‌کردید؟» (آزمایشی). در انگلیسی این تفاوت را will و would نشان می‌دهند."},"wrong":"If we offered 8,500, will you accept it?","right":"If we offered 8,500, would you accept it?"},{"eyebrow":{"en":"Key phrases","tr":"Anahtar ifadeler","fa":"عبارت‌های کلیدی"},"head":{"en":"Phrases for this task","tr":"Bu görev için ifadeler","fa":"عبارت‌های این کار"},"phrases":[{"phrase":"I see where you're coming from.","meaning":{"en":"Shows you understand before you disagree.","tr":"Karşı çıkmadan önce anladığını gösterir.","fa":"پیش از مخالفت، نشان می‌دهد که دلیل طرف را درک می‌کنی."}},{"phrase":"If we..., would you...?","meaning":{"en":"Tests a trade-off.","tr":"Bir ödünleşimi dener.","fa":"یک بده‌بستان را محک می‌زند."}},{"phrase":"So, to confirm: if you..., we will...","meaning":{"en":"Closes with a firm summary.","tr":"Kesin bir özetle kapatır.","fa":"با یک جمع‌بندی قطعی، مذاکره را تمام می‌کند."}}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"At work","tr":"İş yerinde","fa":"در محیط کار"},"head":{"en":"Invite the question","tr":"Soru sormaya kapı aç","fa":"راه سؤال کردن را باز کن"},"body":{"en":"In the UK and US, a polite salary negotiation is normal and offers are rarely withdrawn because of it. Candidates from cultures where questioning an offer feels rude often accept the first number and later feel underpaid. HR can make it easier by asking: \"Is there anything in the offer you would like to discuss?\" Pay bands also protect fairness for people already in the same role.","tr":"Birleşik Krallık'ta ve ABD'de kibar bir maaş pazarlığı normaldir ve teklifler bu yüzden nadiren geri çekilir. Bir teklifi sorgulamanın kaba göründüğü kültürlerden gelen adaylar çoğu zaman ilk sayıyı kabul eder ve sonradan az kazandığını hisseder. İK bunu kolaylaştırmak için şöyle sorabilir: \"Is there anything in the offer you would like to discuss?\" Maaş bantları aynı görevdeki mevcut çalışanlar için de adaleti korur.","fa":"در بریتانیا و آمریکا، مذاکره‌ی مؤدبانه بر سر حقوق کاملاً عادی است و تقریباً هیچ‌وقت پیشنهاد کار به این دلیل پس گرفته نمی‌شود. متقاضیانی که در فرهنگی بزرگ شده‌اند که چانه زدن بر سر پیشنهاد را بی‌ادبی می‌داند، اغلب همان عدد اول را می‌پذیرند و بعدها حس می‌کنند کمتر از حقشان می‌گیرند. منابع انسانی می‌تواند کار را آسان کند و خودش بپرسد: «⁨Is there anything in the offer you would like to discuss?⁩» بازه‌های حقوق هم حق کسانی را حفظ می‌کنند که همین حالا در همان سمت کار می‌کنند."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"From weak to strong","tr":"Zayıftan güçlüye","fa":"از قول زودهنگام تا ایده‌ای که هنوز باز است"},"text":"Facts: They want more pay. One idea you could test: a pay review after six months.","item":"No problem, we'll pay you 9,000.","why":{"en":"Weak: a promise too early. Strong: an idea, not yet a promise.","tr":"Zayıf: çok erken bir söz. Güçlü: bir fikir, henüz söz değil.","fa":"نسخه‌ی اول خیلی زود قول می‌دهد. نسخه‌ی دوم فقط ایده‌ای را مطرح می‌کند و هنوز قولی نمی‌دهد."},"answer":"If we reviewed your pay after six months, would that help?","cut":["No problem, we'll pay you 9,000."],"cutHint":{"en":"Tap the promise made before the idea was tested.","tr":"Fikir denenmeden verilen söze dokun.","fa":"روی قولی بزن که قبل از امتحان کردن ایده داده شده."}},"quick":{"prompt":"A candidate accepts your first offer at once but looks unsure. What can HR ask?","options":["\"Is there anything in the offer you would like to discuss?\"","\"Are you sure? Many people ask for more.\"","\"Great, please sign today.\""],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Invite the question: candidates from cultures where questioning an offer feels rude often accept the first number and later feel underpaid.","tr":"Soruya kapı aç: Bir teklifi sorgulamanın kaba sayıldığı kültürlerden gelen adaylar çoğu zaman ilk rakamı kabul eder ve sonra az ücret aldıklarını düşünür.","fa":"راه سؤال را باز کن: داوطلب‌هایی که از فرهنگ‌هایی می‌آیند که در آن‌ها سؤال کردن درباره‌ی پیشنهاد بی‌ادبی است، اغلب اولین عدد را قبول می‌کنند و بعداً حس می‌کنند حقوقشان کم است."},"point":4},"remember":{"en":"Can you really promise it today? First conditional. Just testing an idea? Second conditional. Result of this lesson: you can negotiate without false promises. You also have the terms confirmed by email.","tr":"Bugün gerçekten söz verebilir misin? Birinci tip koşul. Sadece bir fikri mi deniyorsun? İkinci tip koşul. Bu dersin sonucu: boş söz vermeden pazarlık yapabilirsin ve elinde e-postayla teyit edilmiş koşullar olur.","fa":"واقعاً می‌توانی امروز قولش را بدهی؟ شرطی نوع اول. فقط ایده‌ای را امتحان می‌کنی؟ شرطی نوع دوم. حالا می‌توانی بدون قول بی‌پشتوانه مذاکره کنی. ایمیل تأیید شرایط هم آماده است."},"b2Point":{"eyebrow":{"en":"B2 track","tr":"B2 yolu","fa":"مسیر B2"},"head":{"en":"Hypothetical proposals: what if we were to..., supposing...","tr":"Varsayımsal öneriler: what if we were to..., supposing...","fa":"پیشنهاد فرضی: what if we were to...، supposing..."},"steps":[{"en":"Very tentative: were to + base verb.","tr":"Çok temkinli: were to + yalın fiil.","fa":"برای ایده‌ای خیلی آزمایشی، were to و فعل ساده را به کار ببر.","ex":"What if we were to bring the review forward?"},{"en":"Supposing = if, with a second conditional.","tr":"Supposing = if, ikinci tip koşulla.","fa":"Supposing یعنی if، با شرطی نوع دوم.","ex":"Supposing we agreed to 8,200, would you sign today?"},{"en":"Use were for every person.","tr":"Her kişi için were kullan.","fa":"برای همه‌ی اشخاص were بیاور.","ex":"if I were to / if we were to"}],"table":{"headers":{"en":["Pattern","Example"],"tr":["Kalıp","Örnek"],"fa":["الگو","مثال"]},"rows":[["What if we were to + verb...?","What if we were to bring the review forward?"],["Supposing + past, would...?","Supposing we agreed to 8,200, would you sign today?"],["If I were to + verb...","If I were to accept, when would I start?"]]},"body":{"en":"B2 track: in round 1 or 2, float one idea with \"What if we were to...?\" or \"Supposing..., would...?\" before you make a firm offer.","tr":"B2 yolu: 1. ya da 2. turda kesin bir teklif yapmadan önce \"What if we were to...?\" ya da \"Supposing..., would...?\" ile bir fikir ortaya at.","fa":"مسیر B2: در دور اول یا دوم، پیش از دادن پیشنهاد قطعی، یک ایده را با «⁨What if we were to...?⁩» یا «⁨Supposing..., would...?⁩» مطرح کن."}}},"grammar":{"id":"c-hr-6-2-g","level":"B1","course":"hr","unit":"hr-6-2","title":"Firm offers and tentative proposals: if + will, if + would","titleTr":"Kesin teklifler ve temkinli öneriler: if + will, if + would","exp":{"en":"Negotiation uses two conditionals for two jobs. A firm offer, something you can really promise, uses the first conditional: If + present, will + verb: \"If you start on 1 January, we will pay for your certification.\" A tentative proposal, an idea you are testing, uses the second conditional: If + past, would + verb: \"If we offered 8,500, would you accept it?\" The past form makes it softer and shows that nothing is agreed yet. Do not mix them: not \"If we offered 8,500, will you accept?\", and no will or would in the if-part: not \"If you will start on 1 January\".","tr":"Pazarlık iki iş için iki koşul cümlesi kullanır. Kesin bir teklif, yani gerçekten söz verebileceğin bir şey, first conditional kullanır: If + present, will + fiil: \"If you start on 1 January, we will pay for your certification.\" Temkinli bir öneri, yani denediğin bir fikir, second conditional kullanır: If + past, would + fiil: \"If we offered 8,500, would you accept it?\" Geçmiş biçim cümleyi yumuşatır ve henüz hiçbir şeyin kararlaştırılmadığını gösterir. İkisini karıştırma: \"If we offered 8,500, will you accept?\" değil; if'li kısımda da will ya da would olmaz: \"If you will start on 1 January\" değil.","fa":"در مذاکره از دو نوع جمله‌ی شرطی برای دو کار متفاوت استفاده می‌شود. پیشنهاد قطعی، یعنی چیزی که واقعاً می‌توانی قولش را بدهی، با شرطی نوع اول گفته می‌شود: if + حال ساده، will + فعل: «⁨If you start on 1 January, we will pay for your certification.⁩» پیشنهاد آزمایشی، یعنی ایده‌ای که داری واکنش طرف را به آن می‌سنجی، با شرطی نوع دوم گفته می‌شود: if + گذشته‌ی ساده، would + فعل: «⁨If we offered 8,500, would you accept it?⁩» زمان گذشته اینجا لحن را نرم‌تر می‌کند و نشان می‌دهد هنوز چیزی قطعی نشده است؛ مثل فرق «اگر ۸٬۵۰۰ بدهیم، قبول می‌کنید؟» با «اگر ۸٬۵۰۰ می‌دادیم، قبول می‌کردید؟» در فارسی. این دو را با هم مخلوط نکن: نه «⁨If we offered 8,500, will you accept?⁩». در بخش if هم will یا would نمی‌آید: نه «If you will start on 1 January»."},"formsTable":{"headers":{"en":["Job","Pattern","Example"],"tr":["İşlev","Kalıp","Örnek"],"fa":["کاربرد","الگو","مثال"]},"rows":[["Firm offer","If + present, will + verb","If you start on 1 January, we will pay for the course."],["Tentative proposal","If + past, would + verb","If we offered 8,500, would you accept it?"],["Showing you listened","I see where you're coming from.","I see where you're coming from, but..."]]},"wrong":"If we offered 8,500, will you accept it?","right":"If we offered 8,500, would you accept it?","blank":{"sentence":"If we offered 8,500, ___ you accept it?","word":"would","distractors":["will","did"]},"wrong2":"If you will start on 1 January, we will pay for your certification.","right2":"If you start on 1 January, we will pay for your certification.","blank2":{"sentence":"If you ___ on 1 January, we will pay for your certification.","word":"start","distractors":["will start","would start"]},"expParts":{"tryFrom":"blank","hook":{"en":"Hana asked for 8,500. Leyla could not say yes, so she tested an idea instead: 'If we..., would that help?'","tr":"Hana 8.500 istedi. Leyla evet diyemezdi; bunun yerine bir fikri denedi: 'If we..., would that help?'","fa":"هانا ۸٬۵۰۰ خواست. لیلا نمی‌توانست بله بگوید؛ پس به‌جایش ایده‌ای را امتحان کرد: «⁨If we..., would that help?⁩»"},"tryWhy":{"en":"would: 'If we offered' is past, so the other half takes would. will belongs to the first conditional.","tr":"would: 'If we offered' geçmiş biçimde; bu yüzden öbür yarı would alır. will birinci tip koşula aittir.","fa":"جواب would است: If we offered گذشته است؛ پس بخش دیگر would می‌گیرد. will مال شرطی نوع اول است."},"rule":[{"en":"Firm offer: If + present, will + verb.","tr":"Kesin teklif: If + present, will + fiil.","fa":"برای پیشنهاد قطعی، در بخش if حال ساده بیاور و در بخش دیگر will و فعل ساده.","ex":"If you start on 1 January, we will pay for the course."},{"en":"Testing an idea: If + past, would + verb?","tr":"Bir fikri denemek: If + past, would + fiil?","fa":"برای امتحان کردن یک ایده، در بخش if گذشته بیاور و در بخش دیگر would و فعل ساده.","ex":"If we offered 8,500, would you accept it?"},{"en":"No will or would in the if-part.","tr":"if kısmında will ya da would olmaz.","fa":"در بخش if نه will می‌آید نه ⁨would⁩.","ex":"If you start..., not If you will start..."}],"test":{"en":"Can you really promise it today? First conditional. Just testing an idea? Second conditional.","tr":"Bugün gerçekten söz verebilir misin? Birinci tip koşul. Sadece bir fikri mi deniyorsun? İkinci tip koşul.","fa":"واقعاً می‌توانی امروز قولش را بدهی؟ شرطی نوع اول. فقط ایده‌ای را امتحان می‌کنی؟ شرطی نوع دوم."},"contrast":{"en":"Persian and Turkish make the same firm vs tentative difference (agar bedahim / agar midadim), so the idea is familiar. In English, will marks the firm offer and would the tentative one.","tr":"Türkçede de fark var: 'Başlarsan öderiz' (kesin) ve '8.500 versek kabul eder miydin?' (deneme). İngilizcede bu farkı will ve would taşır.","fa":"فارسی هم همین تفاوت را دارد: «اگر ۸٬۵۰۰ بدهیم، قبول می‌کنید؟» (قطعی‌تر) و «اگر ۸٬۵۰۰ می‌دادیم، قبول می‌کردید؟» (آزمایشی). در انگلیسی این تفاوت را will و would نشان می‌دهند."}},"errorWatch":[{"find":["if you will start","if you will meet","if we would offer","if we would pay","if we would bring","if you would start"],"fix":{"en":"No will or would in the if-part: 'If you start on 1 January, we will...' / 'If we offered..., would you...?'","tr":"if kısmında will ya da would olmaz: 'If you start on 1 January, we will...' / 'If we offered..., would you...?'","fa":"در بخش if نه will می‌آید نه would: «⁨If you start on 1 January, we will...⁩» و «If we offered..., would you...?»"}}]},"b2":{"id":"c-hr-6-2-b2","level":"B2","track":"B2","course":"hr","unit":"hr-6-2","title":"Hypothetical proposals: what if we were to..., supposing...","titleTr":"Varsayımsal öneriler: what if we were to..., supposing...","exp":{"en":"Experienced negotiators float ideas without committing to them. \"What if we were to bring the review forward to six months?\" Were to + verb makes the idea even more hypothetical than the past simple, so the other side can say no without anyone losing face. \"Supposing we agreed to 8,200, would you sign today?\" Supposing works like if in a second conditional. Form traps: were to needs the base verb (\"were to bring\", not \"were bring\" or \"were to brought\"), and use were for every person (\"if I were to\", \"if we were to\").","tr":"Deneyimli müzakereciler bağlanmadan fikir ortaya atar. \"What if we were to bring the review forward to six months?\" Were to + fiil, fikri past simple'dan bile daha varsayımsal yapar; böylece karşı taraf kimse mahcup olmadan hayır diyebilir. \"Supposing we agreed to 8,200, would you sign today?\" Supposing, second conditional'daki if gibi çalışır. Biçim tuzakları: were to yalın fiil ister (\"were to bring\"; \"were bring\" ya da \"were to brought\" değil) ve her kişi için were kullanılır (\"if I were to\", \"if we were to\").","fa":"مذاکره‌کننده‌های باتجربه ایده‌ای را مطرح می‌کنند، بی‌آنکه به آن متعهد شوند. «⁨What if we were to bring the review forward to six months?⁩» ساختار were to + فعل، ایده را حتی فرضی‌تر از گذشته‌ی ساده می‌کند؛ این‌طوری طرف مقابل می‌تواند «نه» بگوید و آبروی هیچ‌کس هم نمی‌رود. «⁨Supposing we agreed to 8,200, would you sign today?⁩» supposing یعنی «فرض کنیم» و مثل if در شرطی نوع دوم عمل می‌کند. تله‌های ساختاری: بعد از were to فعل ساده می‌آید («were to bring»، نه «were bring» و نه «were to brought»)، و برای همه‌ی اشخاص were به کار می‌رود («if I were to»، «if we were to»)."},"formsTable":{"headers":{"en":["Pattern","Example"],"tr":["Kalıp","Örnek"],"fa":["الگو","مثال"]},"rows":[["What if we were to + verb...?","What if we were to bring the review forward?"],["Supposing + past, would...?","Supposing we agreed to 8,200, would you sign today?"],["If I were to + verb...","If I were to accept, when would I start?"]]},"wrong":"If we were bring the review forward, would you accept?","right":"If we were to bring the review forward, would you accept?","blank":{"sentence":"What if we ___ bring the review forward to six months?","word":"were to","distractors":["would to","will to"]},"wrong2":"What if we were to brought the review forward?","right2":"What if we were to bring the review forward?","blank2":{"sentence":"___ we agreed to 8,200, would you sign today?","word":"Supposing","distractors":["Suppose that if","Unless"]},"useIn":{"en":"B2 track: in round 1 or 2, float one idea with \"What if we were to...?\" or \"Supposing..., would...?\" before you make a firm offer.","tr":"B2 yolu: 1. ya da 2. turda kesin bir teklif yapmadan önce \"What if we were to...?\" ya da \"Supposing..., would...?\" ile bir fikir ortaya at.","fa":"مسیر B2: در دور اول یا دوم، پیش از دادن پیشنهاد قطعی، یک ایده را با «⁨What if we were to...?⁩» یا «⁨Supposing..., would...?⁩» مطرح کن."},"exitItem":{"from":"hr-6-2","kind":"blank","prompt":"___ we paid for the course, would you stay two years?","options":["Supposing","Suppose to","If were"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Supposing: 'Supposing' + past tests an idea, like 'What if'. 'Suppose to' is wrong, and 'If were' has no subject.","tr":"Supposing: 'Supposing' + geçmiş, 'What if' gibi bir fikri dener. 'Suppose to' yanlıştır; 'If were'de özne yoktur.","fa":"Supposing درست است، چون Supposing و گذشته مثل What if یک ایده را امتحان می‌کند. suppose to غلط است و if were فاعل ندارد."},"hint2":{"en":"The gap starts an imagined idea, like What if. Which option can start a sentence that way on its own?","tr":"Boşluk, What if gibi hayali bir fikri başlatıyor. Hangi seçenek tek başına bir cümleyi bu şekilde başlatabilir?","fa":"جای خالی یک ایده‌ی فرضی را شروع می‌کند، مثل ⁨What if⁩. کدام گزینه به‌تنهایی می‌تواند جمله را این‌طور شروع کند؟"}},"expParts":{"hook":{"en":"'What if we were to bring the review forward?' An idea the other side can refuse without anyone losing face.","tr":"'What if we were to bring the review forward?' Karşı tarafın kimse mahcup olmadan reddedebileceği bir fikir.","fa":"«⁨What if we were to bring the review forward?⁩» ایده‌ای که طرف مقابل می‌تواند ردش کند بی‌آنکه کسی خجالت بکشد."},"tryWhy":{"en":"Supposing: it works like if in a second conditional. Unless means the opposite.","tr":"Supposing: ikinci tip koşulda if gibi çalışır. Unless tam tersi anlama gelir.","fa":"جواب Supposing است: در شرطی نوع دوم مثل if کار می‌کند. Unless معنای برعکس دارد."},"rule":[{"en":"Very tentative: were to + base verb.","tr":"Çok temkinli: were to + yalın fiil.","fa":"برای ایده‌ای خیلی آزمایشی، were to و فعل ساده را به کار ببر.","ex":"What if we were to bring the review forward?"},{"en":"Supposing = if, with a second conditional.","tr":"Supposing = if, ikinci tip koşulla.","fa":"Supposing یعنی if، با شرطی نوع دوم.","ex":"Supposing we agreed to 8,200, would you sign today?"},{"en":"Use were for every person.","tr":"Her kişi için were kullan.","fa":"برای همه‌ی اشخاص were بیاور.","ex":"if I were to / if we were to"}],"test":{"en":"After were, look for to + base verb (to bring). Missing to, or a past form after it? Fix it.","tr":"were'den sonra to + yalın fiil ara (to bring). to eksik mi ya da ardından geçmiş biçim mi var? Düzelt.","fa":"بعد از were دنبال to و فعل ساده بگرد (to bring). to جا افتاده یا بعدش فعل گذشته آمده؟ درستش کن."},"contrast":{"en":"Turkish 'öne çeksek nasıl olur?' and Persian 'age ... jelo biandazim chi?' are already soft. English were to adds one more layer of 'just an idea'.","tr":"Türkçedeki 'Değerlendirmeyi öne çeksek nasıl olur?' zaten yumuşaktır. İngilizcede were to, 'sadece bir fikir' katmanını bir kat daha ekler.","fa":"در فارسی می‌گوییم «اگر بازبینی را جلو بیندازیم چطور است؟» که خودش نرم است. در انگلیسی were to این حس را قوی‌تر می‌کند که «فقط یک ایده است»."}},"errorWatch":[{"find":["were bring","were to brought","were to brings","were to agreed","suppose that if"],"fix":{"en":"Use were to + base verb: 'What if we were to bring the review forward?'","tr":"were to + yalın fiil kullan: 'What if we were to bring the review forward?'","fa":"از were to و فعل ساده استفاده کن: «What if we were to bring the review forward?»"}}]},"vocab":{"id":"c-hr-6-2-v","level":"B1","category":"vocab","course":"hr","unit":"hr-6-2","goals":["career"],"title":{"en":"Negotiating","tr":"Pazarlık","fa":"مذاکره"},"cards":[{"word":"negotiate","sentence":"Hana wanted to negotiate the basic salary.","meaning":{"en":"To discuss in order to reach an agreement.","tr":"pazarlık etmek, müzakere etmek.","fa":"مذاکره کردن"}},{"word":"counter-offer","sentence":"She made a counter-offer of 8,500.","meaning":{"en":"An offer made in reply to another offer.","tr":"karşı teklif.","fa":"پیشنهاد متقابل"}},{"word":"trade-off","sentence":"A shorter review was the trade-off for a lower basic.","meaning":{"en":"Giving one thing to get another.","tr":"ödünleşim, karşılıklı taviz.","fa":"بده‌بستان؛ چیزی دادن برای گرفتن چیز دیگر"}},{"word":"pay band","sentence":"The role's pay band is 7,500 to 8,200 basic.","meaning":{"en":"The fixed range of pay for a type of job.","tr":"maaş bandı.","fa":"بازه‌ی حقوق (کف و سقف ثابت حقوق برای یک نوع شغل)"}},{"word":"bring forward","sentence":"We can bring the review forward to six months.","gap":"bring the review forward","accept":["bring the review forward","bring forward the review","bring forward"],"meaning":{"en":"To move something to an earlier time.","tr":"öne çekmek.","fa":"جلو انداختن (زمان چیزی)"}},{"word":"compromise","sentence":"In the end they reached a compromise.","meaning":{"en":"An agreement where both sides give a little.","tr":"uzlaşma.","fa":"توافق میانه؛ مصالحه (هر دو طرف کمی کوتاه می‌آیند)"}},{"word":"meet someone halfway","sentence":"Can we meet you halfway on the start date?","gap":"meet you halfway","accept":["meet you halfway","meet someone halfway"],"meaning":{"en":"To give part of what someone asks for.","tr":"orta yolda buluşmak.","fa":"با کسی کنار آمدن؛ بخشی از خواسته‌اش را پذیرفتن"}},{"word":"deal-breaker","sentence":"Family insurance was a deal-breaker for her.","meaning":{"en":"Something so important that without it there is no deal.","tr":"anlaşmayı bozacak şart.","fa":"خط قرمز؛ شرطی که بدون آن توافقی در کار نیست"}},{"word":"final offer","sentence":"This is our final offer.","meaning":{"en":"The last offer; no more changes.","tr":"son teklif.","fa":"پیشنهاد نهایی"}},{"word":"I see where you're coming from","sentence":"I see where you're coming from, but the band is fixed.","meaning":{"en":"I understand your reasons.","tr":"Ne demek istediğini anlıyorum.","fa":"دلیلت را درک می‌کنم؛ می‌فهمم چرا این را می‌گویی"}}]},"story":{"id":"c-hr-6-2-s","level":"B1","genre":"Workplace","course":"hr","unit":"hr-6-2","title":{"en":"The Question That Started With \"If\"","tr":"\"Eğer\" ile Başlayan Soru","fa":"سؤالی که با «اگر» شروع شد"},"text":"\"If you could raise the basic to 8,500,\" Hana said, \"I would sign this week.\"\n\nLeyla had expected it. She had also checked the pay band that morning: 7,500 to 8,200 for the role. Three coordinators already worked at Atlas on that band. If she paid Hana 8,500, she would have three unhappy coordinators by Friday.\n\n\"I see where you're coming from,\" she said. \"Dunes Freight's basic is higher, and the gratuity follows the basic. That's a fair point. I can't go above the band. But let me ask you something. If we brought your first salary review forward from twelve months to six, would that help?\"\n\nHana thought. \"Only if the review is real. A review can say zero.\"\n\nIt was a good answer. Leyla wrote it down.\n\n\"What if the six-month review came with a clear target?\" Leyla asked. \"If you meet the cold-chain targets we agree in January, the increase is 5%. Written in the offer.\"\n\n\"And the basic now?\"\n\n\"8,200. The top of the band.\"\n\nThere was a long pause. Leyla did not fill it. She had learned that from Omar, who never filled a silence in his life.\n\n\"One more thing,\" Hana said. \"There's a cold-chain certification course in February. It costs 4,000 dirhams. It would make me better at this job.\"\n\nLeyla checked the training budget on her second screen. \"If you start on 1 January, we will pay for the course.\"\n\nHana laughed for the first time in the call. \"Then I think we have a deal.\"\n\nAfter the call Leyla wrote one line in her notebook: she didn't win, I didn't win, the job won.","vocab":[{"word":"raise","en":"To make higher.","tr":"yükseltmek, artırmak","fa":"بالا بردن؛ افزایش دادن"},{"word":"band","en":"Here: a range of pay between a minimum and a maximum.","tr":"aralık, bant","fa":"بازه (فاصله‌ی بین کف و سقف حقوق)"},{"word":"fill a silence","en":"To speak just because nobody is speaking.","tr":"sessizliği doldurmak","fa":"فقط برای شکستن سکوت حرف زدن"},{"word":"certification","en":"An official course and document that proves a skill.","tr":"sertifika (programı)","fa":"گواهینامه‌ی تخصصی (دوره‌ی رسمی و مدرکی که مهارتی را تأیید می‌کند)"},{"word":"deal","en":"An agreement, especially in business.","tr":"anlaşma","fa":"توافق؛ معامله"}],"quiz":[{"prompt":"Why could Leyla not pay 8,500 basic?","options":["Omar said no","It was above the pay band and unfair to the other coordinators","Hana asked for too little"],"correct":1},{"prompt":"Choose the correct proposal.","options":["If we brought the review forward, would that help?","If we brought the review forward, will that help?","If we would bring the review forward, will that help?"],"correct":0},{"prompt":"What did both sides get in the end?","options":["8,500 basic and no review","8,200 basic, a six-month review with a target, and a paid course","Nothing; Hana chose Dunes Freight"],"correct":1},{"prompt":"What did Hana mean by \"A review can say zero\"?","options":["She was worried a review might give no real increase","She did not want a review","She was joking about maths"],"correct":0}],"notice":{"en":"Hana asks for 8,500 and Leyla cannot pay it. Count the ideas Leyla offers instead. Which one is a promise?","tr":"Hana 8.500 istiyor ve Leyla bunu ödeyemez. Leyla'nın onun yerine sunduğu fikirleri say. Hangisi bir söz?","fa":"هانا ۸٬۵۰۰ می‌خواهد و لیلا نمی‌تواند بپردازد. ایده‌هایی را که لیلا به‌جایش پیشنهاد می‌دهد بشمار. کدام یکی قول است؟"},"bridge":{"en":"'If we brought your review forward, would that help?' and 'If you start on 1 January, we will pay.' Next: see why one says would and one says will.","tr":"'If we brought your review forward, would that help?' ve 'If you start on 1 January, we will pay.' Sırada: birinin neden would, diğerinin neden will dediğini gör.","fa":"«⁨If we brought your review forward, would that help?⁩» و «⁨If you start on 1 January, we will pay.⁩» قدم بعد: ببین چرا یکی would دارد و دیگری ⁨will⁩."}},"speaking":{"id":"hr-6-2","course":"hr","unit":"hr-6-2","topic":{"en":"Negotiating an Offer from Both Sides","tr":"Bir Teklif Üzerinde İki Taraftan Pazarlık","fa":"مذاکره بر سر پیشنهاد کار، از هر دو طرف میز"},"warmup":{"en":"Have you ever negotiated something important (a salary, a rent, a price)? What did you give, and what did you get?","tr":"Hiç önemli bir şeyin (maaş, kira, fiyat) pazarlığını yaptın mı? Ne verdin, ne aldın?","fa":"تا حالا بر سر چیز مهمی (حقوق، اجاره، قیمت) مذاکره کرده‌ای؟ چه چیزی دادی و چه چیزی گرفتی؟"},"questions":[{"en":"Round 1, you are HR: Hana says \"I need 8,500 basic.\" Show you understand, explain the limit, and propose a trade-off with \"If we..., would you...?\"","tr":"1. tur, sen İK'sın: Hana \"8.500 temel maaşa ihtiyacım var\" diyor. Anladığını göster, sınırı açıkla ve \"If we..., would you...?\" ile bir ödünleşim öner.","fa":"دور اول، تو نماینده‌ی منابع انسانی هستی: هانا می‌گوید «⁨I need 8,500 basic.⁩» نشان بده که حرفش را می‌فهمی، محدودیت را توضیح بده و با «⁨If we..., would you...?⁩» یک بده‌بستان پیشنهاد کن."},{"en":"Round 2, you are Hana: answer HR's proposal and make one counter-proposal with \"What if...?\"","tr":"2. tur, sen Hana'sın: İK'nın önerisine cevap ver ve \"What if...?\" ile bir karşı öneri yap.","fa":"دور دوم، تو هانا هستی: به پیشنهاد منابع انسانی جواب بده و با «⁨What if...?⁩» یک پیشنهاد متقابل بده."},{"en":"Round 3, either side: summarise the deal with one firm offer: \"If you..., we will...\".","tr":"3. tur, herhangi bir taraf: anlaşmayı kesin bir teklifle özetle: \"If you..., we will...\".","fa":"دور سوم، از هر طرف که می‌خواهی: توافق را با یک پیشنهاد قطعی جمع‌بندی کن: «⁨If you..., we will...⁩»."}],"followups":[{"en":"Repeat round 1 in 90 seconds, then 60, then 45.","tr":"1. turu 90, sonra 60, sonra 45 saniyede tekrarla.","fa":"دور اول را یک بار در ۹۰ ثانیه، بعد در ۶۰ و بعد در ۴۵ ثانیه تکرار کن."},{"en":"Now make one real offer with if: what could you give, and what would you need?","tr":"Şimdi if ile gerçek bir teklif yap: ne verebilirsin, karşılığında neye ihtiyacın var?","fa":"حالا با if یک پیشنهاد واقعی بده: چه می‌توانی بدهی و در عوض به چه نیاز داری؟"}],"expressions":[{"phrase":"I see where you're coming from.","meaning":{"en":"Shows you understand before you disagree.","tr":"Karşı çıkmadan önce anladığını gösterir.","fa":"پیش از مخالفت، نشان می‌دهد که دلیل طرف را درک می‌کنی."}},{"phrase":"If we..., would you...?","meaning":{"en":"Tests a trade-off.","tr":"Bir ödünleşimi dener.","fa":"یک بده‌بستان را محک می‌زند."}},{"phrase":"So, to confirm: if you..., we will...","meaning":{"en":"Closes with a firm summary.","tr":"Kesin bir özetle kapatır.","fa":"با یک جمع‌بندی قطعی، مذاکره را تمام می‌کند."}}],"culture":{"en":"In the UK and US, a polite salary negotiation is normal and offers are rarely withdrawn because of it. Candidates from cultures where questioning an offer feels rude often accept the first number and later feel underpaid. HR can make it easier by asking: \"Is there anything in the offer you would like to discuss?\" Pay bands also protect fairness for people already in the same role.","tr":"Birleşik Krallık'ta ve ABD'de kibar bir maaş pazarlığı normaldir ve teklifler bu yüzden nadiren geri çekilir. Bir teklifi sorgulamanın kaba göründüğü kültürlerden gelen adaylar çoğu zaman ilk sayıyı kabul eder ve sonradan az kazandığını hisseder. İK bunu kolaylaştırmak için şöyle sorabilir: \"Is there anything in the offer you would like to discuss?\" Maaş bantları aynı görevdeki mevcut çalışanlar için de adaleti korur.","fa":"در بریتانیا و آمریکا، مذاکره‌ی مؤدبانه بر سر حقوق کاملاً عادی است و تقریباً هیچ‌وقت پیشنهاد کار به این دلیل پس گرفته نمی‌شود. متقاضیانی که در فرهنگی بزرگ شده‌اند که چانه زدن بر سر پیشنهاد را بی‌ادبی می‌داند، اغلب همان عدد اول را می‌پذیرند و بعدها حس می‌کنند کمتر از حقشان می‌گیرند. منابع انسانی می‌تواند کار را آسان کند و خودش بپرسد: «⁨Is there anything in the offer you would like to discuss?⁩» بازه‌های حقوق هم حق کسانی را حفظ می‌کنند که همین حالا در همان سمت کار می‌کنند."},"model":"I see where you're coming from. Dunes Freight's basic is higher, and that's a fair point. I can't go above the band, which is 8,200. But if we brought your first review forward from twelve months to six, would that help? And what if the review came with a clear target? So, to confirm: if you start on 1 January, we will pay for your certification course.","selfCheck":[{"en":"I showed I understood before I explained the limit.","tr":"Sınırı açıklamadan önce anladığımı gösterdim.","fa":"پیش از توضیح محدودیت، نشان دادم که حرفش را فهمیده‌ام."},{"en":"I tested an idea with 'If we..., would you...?'","tr":"Bir fikri 'If we..., would you...?' ile denedim.","fa":"یک ایده را با «⁨If we..., would you...?⁩» امتحان کردم."},{"en":"I made one firm offer with 'If you..., we will...'","tr":"'If you..., we will...' ile kesin bir teklif yaptım.","fa":"یک پیشنهاد قطعی با «⁨If you..., we will...⁩» دادم."},{"en":"I let a silence happen instead of filling it.","tr":"Sessizliği doldurmak yerine olmasına izin verdim.","fa":"به‌جای پر کردن سکوت، گذاشتم سکوت بماند."}]},"writing":{"id":"c-hr-6-2-w","title":{"en":"Confirming Hana's terms","tr":"Hana'nın koşullarını teyit etmek","fa":"تأیید شرایط هانا"},"course":"hr","unit":"hr-6-2","type":"writing","difficulty":"medium","prompt":{"en":"Write the email to Hana confirming the agreed terms (60-90 words): basic salary, the six-month review and its target, the paid course with its condition, and the next step.","tr":"Hana'ya kararlaştırılan koşulları teyit eden e-postayı yaz (60-90 kelime): temel maaş, altı aylık değerlendirme ve hedefi, koşuluyla birlikte ücretli kurs ve sonraki adım.","fa":"ایمیلی برای هانا بنویس و شرایط توافق‌شده را تأیید کن (۶۰ تا ۹۰ کلمه): حقوق پایه، بازبینی شش‌ماهه و هدفش، دوره‌ای که شرکت هزینه‌اش را می‌دهد و شرط آن و قدم بعدی."},"model":"Dear Hana, Thank you for a very open conversation today. To confirm what we agreed: your basic salary will be 8,200 dirhams a month. Your first salary review will take place after six months, and if you meet the cold-chain targets we agree in January, your basic will rise by 5%. If you start on 1 January, Atlas will pay for the certification course in February. I will send the updated offer letter by Thursday. Kind regards, Leyla","frame":"Dear ___, Thank you for ___. To confirm what we agreed: your basic salary will be ___. Your first salary review will take place after ___, and if you ___, your basic will rise by ___. If you start on ___, Atlas will ___. I will send ___ by ___. Kind regards, ___","words":[{"word":"to confirm"},{"word":"if you"},{"word":"will"}],"minWords":60,"minSentences":5,"rubric":["Task done: basic, review, target, course and condition, next step","Organised: one term per sentence","Language: first conditional for firm terms; by + date","Tone: warm and exact; nothing left vague"],"rubricI18n":{"tr":["Görev: temel maaş, gözden geçirme, hedef, kurs ve şartı, sonraki adım","Düzen: her cümlede bir şart","Dil: kesin şartlar için first conditional; by + tarih","Üslup: sıcak ve kesin; belirsiz bir şey kalmamış"],"fa":["کامل بودن کار: حقوق پایه، بازبینی، هدف، دوره و شرطش، قدم بعدی","نظم: در هر جمله یک بند از توافق","زبان: شرطی نوع اول برای شرط‌های قطعی؛ by با تاریخ","لحن: گرم و دقیق؛ هیچ چیز مبهم نمانده"]},"portfolio":null,"parts":[{"t":{"en":"The basic salary","tr":"Temel maaş","fa":"حقوق پایه"},"find":["basic salary","will be"],"sample":"8,200 dirhams a month"},{"t":{"en":"The review and its target","tr":"Değerlendirme ve hedefi","fa":"بازبینی و هدفش"},"find":["review","targets","after six months"],"sample":"review after six months; +5% if the cold-chain targets are met"},{"t":{"en":"The course and its condition","tr":"Kurs ve koşulu","fa":"دوره و شرطش"},"find":["if you start","course"],"sample":"course in February if she starts on 1 January"},{"t":{"en":"The next step","tr":"Sonraki adım","fa":"قدم بعدی"},"find":["i will send","by thursday"],"sample":"the updated offer letter by Thursday"}]},"perspective":{"id":"c-hr-6-2-p","title":{"en":"Hana before saying yes","tr":"Evet demeden önce Hana","fa":"هانا پیش از «بله» گفتن"},"course":"hr","unit":"hr-6-2","type":"perspective","minSentences":2,"prompt":{"en":"You played both sides. Now write as Hana, 2-3 sentences in first person: what did you need to hear from HR before you could say yes?","tr":"İki tarafı da oynadın. Şimdi Hana olarak birinci tekil şahısla 2-3 cümle yaz: evet diyebilmek için İK'dan ne duymaya ihtiyacın vardı?","fa":"تو هر دو طرف را بازی کردی. حالا از زبان هانا دو یا سه جمله بنویس: پیش از اینکه بتوانی «بله» بگویی، لازم بود چه چیزی از منابع انسانی بشنوی؟"}},"exit":{"id":"c-hr-6-2-x","course":"hr","unit":"hr-6-2","type":"exit","items":[{"from":"hr-6-2","kind":"blank","prompt":"If we ___ 8,300, would that work for you?","options":["would offer","offered","will offer"],"correct":1,"point":2,"why":{"en":"offered: a tentative proposal takes if + past, then would. 'Would offer' and 'will offer' can't follow if here.","tr":"offered: kararsız bir öneri if + geçmiş, sonra would alır. 'Would offer' ve 'will offer' burada if'ten sonra gelmez.","fa":"offered درست است، چون پیشنهاد آزمایشی با if و گذشته می‌آید و بعد would. would offer و will offer اینجا بعد از if نمی‌آیند."}},{"from":"hr-6-2","kind":"blank","prompt":"If you sign today, we ___ your visa next week.","options":["will start","would started","started"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"will start: a firm offer takes if + present, then will + plain verb. 'Would started' is wrong twice, and 'started' doesn't fit the result.","tr":"will start: kesin bir teklif if + geniş zaman, sonra will + yalın fiil alır. 'Would started' iki kez yanlıştır; 'started' sonuç kısmına uymaz.","fa":"will start درست است، چون پیشنهاد قطعی با if و حال ساده و بعد will و فعل ساده می‌آید. would started دو اشتباه دارد و started با بخش نتیجه جور نیست."}},{"from":"hr-6-2","kind":"mcq","prompt":"Which line shows you understand before you disagree?","options":["That's impossible.","I see where you're coming from, but the band is fixed.","Take it or leave it."],"correct":1,"point":3,"why":{"en":"'I see where you're coming from, but the band is fixed' shows you understood, then gives the limit. 'That's impossible' and 'Take it or leave it' close the talk.","tr":"'I see where you're coming from, but the band is fixed' anladığını gösterir, sonra sınırı söyler. 'That's impossible' ve 'Take it or leave it' konuşmayı kapatır.","fa":"«I see where you're coming from, but the band is fixed» نشان می‌دهد فهمیده‌ای و بعد حد را می‌گوید. That's impossible و Take it or leave it گفتگو را می‌بندند."},"hint2":{"en":"Look for the line that first shows you see their point, and only then gives the limit.","tr":"Önce karşındakinin bakış açısını anladığını gösteren, ancak ondan sonra sınırı söyleyen satırı ara.","fa":"دنبال خطی بگرد که اول نشان بدهد حرفش را می‌فهمی و فقط بعد از آن محدودیت را بگوید."}},{"from":"hr-6-1","kind":"blank","prompt":"Your basic salary rises ___ 8,400 dirhams after one year.","options":["by","to","with"],"correct":1,"point":2,"why":{"en":"to: 'rises to' + the new amount. 'By' would give the size of the rise, and 'with' doesn't measure change.","tr":"to: 'rises to' + yeni tutar. 'By' artışın miktarını verir; 'with' değişimi ölçmez.","fa":"to درست است، چون rises to و بعد مبلغ جدید. by مقدار افزایش را می‌گوید و with تغییر را نمی‌سنجد."},"hint2":{"en":"8,400 is the new amount, not the size of the rise. Which word goes before a new amount?","tr":"8.400 yeni miktar, artışın büyüklüğü değil. Yeni bir miktardan önce hangi kelime gelir?","fa":"۸٬۴۰۰ مقدار جدید است، نه اندازه‌ی افزایش. قبل از مقدار جدید کدام کلمه می‌آید؟"}},{"from":"hr-5-3","kind":"blank","prompt":"Since January you ___ two new drivers.","options":["have trained","trained","are training"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"have trained: 'since January' runs until now, so the present perfect. 'Trained' is for finished time, and 'are training' doesn't go with since.","tr":"have trained: 'since January' bugüne kadar sürer, bu yüzden present perfect. 'Trained' bitmiş zaman içindir; 'are training' since ile kullanılmaz.","fa":"have trained درست است، چون since January تا الان ادامه دارد و حال کامل می‌خواهد. trained برای زمان تمام‌شده است و are training با since نمی‌آید."}},{"from":"hr-2-3","kind":"blank","prompt":"Could you tell me ___ you are available from January?","options":["do","are","if"],"correct":2,"point":2,"why":{"en":"if: it opens an indirect yes/no question. 'Do' and 'are' can't sit inside the sentence this way.","tr":"if: dolaylı bir evet/hayır sorusu açar. 'Do' ve 'are' cümlenin içinde bu şekilde yer alamaz.","fa":"if درست است، چون سؤال بله‌یا‌نهِ غیرمستقیم را باز می‌کند. do و are این‌طور داخل جمله نمی‌آیند."}},{"from":"hr-6-2","kind":"mcq","prompt":"A candidate asks for more pay, and you are not sure the budget allows it. Which sentence keeps your options open?","options":["If we added a review after three months, would that work for you?","Yes, we will pay you more.","We can never change the offer."],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"The first tests an idea without promising it. Use would for an idea you are testing, and will only for a promise you can keep.","tr":"İlki söz vermeden bir fikri dener. Denediğin bir fikir için would, yalnızca tutabileceğin bir söz için will kullan.","fa":"گزینه‌ی اول بدون قول دادن یک ایده را امتحان می‌کند. برای ایده‌ای که امتحان می‌کنی ⁨would⁩ بگو و ⁨will⁩ را فقط برای قولی که می‌توانی نگه داری."},"point":1}]}}; })(globalThis.COURSE_FILES = globalThis.COURSE_FILES || {});
